WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.404 --> 00:00:03.051
- Hey guys, welcome to Is This Okay,

00:00:03.051 --> 00:00:04.653
where we talk about
things that are happening

00:00:04.653 --> 00:00:06.658
in the world, wondering if, it's okay.

00:00:06.658 --> 00:00:07.658
I'm Nyla.

00:00:07.658 --> 00:00:08.658
- I'm Becky.

00:00:08.658 --> 00:00:09.664
- I'm Daysha.

00:00:09.664 --> 00:00:10.666
- I'm Morgan.

00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:11.665
- I'm Kwesi.

00:00:11.665 --> 00:00:13.151
- Yeah, Kwesi.

00:00:13.151 --> 00:00:15.401
(giggling)

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:18.200
- I just realized it's like The View,

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.033
with a male guest.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.116
- [All] Yeah.

00:00:21.613 --> 00:00:22.552
- So today, we're gonna talk about

00:00:22.552 --> 00:00:24.304
how do you separate the
person from their art,

00:00:24.304 --> 00:00:26.457
when the person can
sometimes be problematic

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:29.231
in their life, but the work that they've

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:31.725
done is really important,
or something that's

00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:32.935
very valuable.

00:00:32.935 --> 00:00:35.743
What sparked this
discussion was Nate Parker,

00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:37.161
and Birth of a Nation.

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:39.634
- You have Nate Parker, who
took this very important

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.979
slave revolt story, and so this is a very

00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:43.674
monumental film for the black community.

00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:47.713
But, 17 years ago, Nate
Parker was caught up

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.130
in a rape charge, allegation.

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:53.140
- I think he was acquitted
of rape, essentially.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.199
- Yeah.

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:55.449
- 17 years ago.

00:00:55.449 --> 00:00:56.998
- I think the reason why
the question or discussion

00:00:56.998 --> 00:00:59.888
of today is more about
a broader scope of it,

00:00:59.888 --> 00:01:01.616
is because with any one of
these particular things,

00:01:01.616 --> 00:01:03.779
you never can know exactly for sure

00:01:03.779 --> 00:01:05.283
if the person did it.

00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:06.285
- It happened.

00:01:06.285 --> 00:01:09.858
And this woman is not here anymore,

00:01:09.858 --> 00:01:12.219
to talk about what happened.

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:15.505
And she's not here as a result

00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:16.338
of that experience.

00:01:16.338 --> 00:01:18.091
- He wrote a letter about that as well,

00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:19.893
I think, showing empathy.

00:01:19.893 --> 00:01:22.270
- He has not shown an ounce

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.933
of empathy.

00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:25.768
He's just like, I'm not gonna say sorry,

00:01:25.768 --> 00:01:27.626
it sucks that that happened to you,

00:01:27.626 --> 00:01:28.798
or you think that's what happened to you,

00:01:28.798 --> 00:01:30.551
but I'm not going to apologize.

00:01:30.551 --> 00:01:33.442
I was leaning towards,
this film is important,

00:01:33.442 --> 00:01:35.323
so like, I'll probably go see it.

00:01:35.323 --> 00:01:36.983
And then I read the
article where he's like,

00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:38.005
"I'm not sayin' sorry."

00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:39.479
And I was like, well now I'm
all up in my feels again,

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:40.883
and I don't know how I feel.

00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:41.884
(laughs)

00:01:41.884 --> 00:01:43.392
- Well, I'm gonna go
see the movie for sure.

00:01:43.392 --> 00:01:45.516
Nate Parker is not my friend,

00:01:45.516 --> 00:01:48.663
you know, he's someone who
put something on screen,

00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:50.437
that I think is important to see.

00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:52.831
- Where do you personally
draw the line between,

00:01:52.831 --> 00:01:56.384
I like your art, but
you're a shitty person?

00:01:56.384 --> 00:01:58.392
What is considered
supporting, like I know people

00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:00.168
who were like, "I don't turn
Chris Brown off in the car,

00:02:00.168 --> 00:02:02.932
"if it's on the radio, but
I won't buy his albums."

00:02:02.932 --> 00:02:04.719
- I'm like that with hip hop in general.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:07.459
Like, for me, I'm not
going to pay for the music,

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:09.964
I'm not gonna give someone
money to take that money

00:02:09.964 --> 00:02:12.661
and then oppress me, but,
if it's there, like I'm

00:02:12.661 --> 00:02:14.333
not gonna throw a hissy fit about it.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.898
- When we say, like, support
an artist, we probably

00:02:16.898 --> 00:02:21.062
mean, in some way, buying
the song, going to a concert,

00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:23.632
I would continue to
purchase Michael Jackson

00:02:23.632 --> 00:02:25.095
songs on iTunes.

00:02:25.095 --> 00:02:27.753
I feel a little weird
about that sometimes.

00:02:27.753 --> 00:02:28.822
- But was he convicted?

00:02:28.822 --> 00:02:30.459
- He wasn't though.

00:02:30.459 --> 00:02:31.463
- Exactly.

00:02:31.463 --> 00:02:32.537
That's the weird part, right?

00:02:32.537 --> 00:02:34.986
It's like, because someone
with so power and so much

00:02:34.986 --> 00:02:37.768
influence, but then again,
he could be someone who

00:02:37.768 --> 00:02:39.712
did something so horribly wrong.

00:02:39.712 --> 00:02:41.523
- If you're trying to
debate with yourself,

00:02:41.523 --> 00:02:43.272
whether or not, to
like, go see that movie,

00:02:43.272 --> 00:02:46.144
or like, go see that artist
that you know did something,

00:02:46.144 --> 00:02:48.361
then are you background
checking every artist

00:02:48.361 --> 00:02:49.882
that you support?

00:02:49.882 --> 00:02:51.677
- All situations are totally different,

00:02:51.677 --> 00:02:53.070
and then again, I don't
have like, the facts

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.095
on the Nate Parker story.

00:02:54.095 --> 00:02:56.383
Something terrible happened for sure.

00:02:56.383 --> 00:02:58.986
- Is there an artist that
you can think of that's

00:02:58.986 --> 00:03:01.572
done something that, in your opinion,

00:03:01.572 --> 00:03:04.671
you still feel okay supporting their work?

00:03:04.671 --> 00:03:07.239
- I saw The Pianist that Polansky did.

00:03:07.239 --> 00:03:08.876
- Yeah.

00:03:08.876 --> 00:03:10.467
- Didn't know Polanksy
did the things he did.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.298
Right, it's like, man,
that's a horrible person.

00:03:12.298 --> 00:03:13.416
The Pianist was a dope film.

00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:15.819
- And like, here's the
thing though, for me,

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:17.823
is that like, it's one
thing if you're not aware

00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:20.208
of someone doing something terrible,

00:03:20.208 --> 00:03:21.969
and you've already supported the art,

00:03:21.969 --> 00:03:23.480
that's one thing.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.293
But it's hard for me to
consciously know what has

00:03:25.293 --> 00:03:27.394
happened, and then still
feel like I can support that.

00:03:27.394 --> 00:03:29.811
- You wanna see some remorse.

00:03:31.094 --> 00:03:35.088
Like Roman Polansky, emailed
his victim years later,

00:03:35.088 --> 00:03:36.763
and apologized.

00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:39.071
- I wonder how much more
comfortable I would be

00:03:39.071 --> 00:03:41.605
going to see it if he
just spoke more openly

00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:43.357
and sensitively about it.

00:03:43.357 --> 00:03:45.110
- I think that, especially
as a black person,

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.922
it's really hard, cause
I feel like at the end

00:03:46.922 --> 00:03:49.230
of the day, when it's a black figure,

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.391
I'm forced to choose between my blackness,

00:03:51.391 --> 00:03:53.795
or like, supporting a fucked up thing.

00:03:53.795 --> 00:03:55.986
- When Tyra Banks was like,
"we were all rooting for you!"

00:03:55.986 --> 00:03:57.394
Like, that's how I felt.

00:03:57.394 --> 00:03:58.774
- Yes, I feel that!

00:03:58.774 --> 00:03:59.774
(extreme crosstalk)

00:03:59.774 --> 00:04:02.221
- That's how I felt, I was just like, no!

00:04:02.221 --> 00:04:03.908
Are you kidding me?

00:04:03.908 --> 00:04:06.519
We were all rooting for you,
and the thing about it is,

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:09.062
I was so ready, I was like, yes!

00:04:09.062 --> 00:04:11.164
People are excited about
it because it's educational

00:04:11.164 --> 00:04:13.532
and it's about black folk,
who are unapologetic,

00:04:13.532 --> 00:04:15.401
and that's something that we need today.

00:04:15.401 --> 00:04:18.024
But then, this came up, and
I'm like, there's no way

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.720
that I can support this.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.473
- I felt this way about
Straight Outta Compton, too,

00:04:21.473 --> 00:04:24.829
like, you know, I was so
here for it, especially

00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:26.117
as someone who loves hip
hop, and then to find

00:04:26.117 --> 00:04:29.553
out about all the Dr.
Dre and the woman beating

00:04:29.553 --> 00:04:32.050
things, and the casting
call, and I was like,

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:34.614
I can't, I can't give you my money,

00:04:34.614 --> 00:04:36.331
because again, money is power.

00:04:36.331 --> 00:04:37.866
- There also needs to be more grey.

00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:39.572
It was actually a really
wise thing that Daysha said.

00:04:39.572 --> 00:04:41.710
I was like telling her
that I was really upset

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.121
about something Beyonce
did, I felt bad about that,

00:04:44.121 --> 00:04:46.701
because I still like
Beyonce, and Daysha was like,

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:48.835
"You can like her as an
artist, and a person,

00:04:48.835 --> 00:04:51.137
"and not be okay with
everything that she does."

00:04:51.137 --> 00:04:52.809
- It's hard too, because
like, his one terrible

00:04:52.809 --> 00:04:55.885
mistake is a reflection upon everybody who

00:04:55.885 --> 00:04:58.423
was a part of the film.

00:04:58.423 --> 00:05:00.692
So like, people are choosing
not to see it, like me.

00:05:00.692 --> 00:05:03.535
I'm well aware that I am
not supporting the cast,

00:05:03.535 --> 00:05:05.429
the crew, you know, everyone else.

00:05:05.429 --> 00:05:07.769
And a part of me is like,
damn that sucks, because,

00:05:07.769 --> 00:05:10.732
I want, yeah, like I love Gabrielle Union.

00:05:10.732 --> 00:05:13.807
You know, I'm sure the
crew worked hard, they were

00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:15.849
like, you know, this was a long journey.

00:05:15.849 --> 00:05:17.445
- You can always argue
that you going to see

00:05:17.445 --> 00:05:19.404
the movie doesn't make
that much of a difference,

00:05:19.404 --> 00:05:21.137
but it's just that much more admirable,

00:05:21.137 --> 00:05:25.143
to take your own personal
stand against it.

00:05:25.143 --> 00:05:26.663
- I'm gonna go see the film.

00:05:26.663 --> 00:05:28.382
What I can take away
from this is learn from

00:05:28.382 --> 00:05:29.612
the situation.

00:05:29.612 --> 00:05:31.363
- I mean, I think it's a
pretty fucked situation.

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:32.383
- Yeah.

00:05:32.383 --> 00:05:33.744
- I think that Birth of
a Nation is gonna be an

00:05:33.744 --> 00:05:35.984
incredibly important
film, and I think that

00:05:35.984 --> 00:05:39.984
it's really fucked that
it's entrenched in this,

00:05:41.928 --> 00:05:43.242
in this tragedy.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.248
- Are you gonna see it?

00:05:44.248 --> 00:05:45.444
- I'm gonna Netflix it.

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:46.897
- I love how we act like
that's really sticking

00:05:46.897 --> 00:05:47.921
it to them.

00:05:47.921 --> 00:05:48.920
- I am.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.727
I'm gonna Netflix that movie!

00:05:50.727 --> 00:05:51.729
(laughing)

00:05:51.729 --> 00:05:53.065
I can't separate art from artists.

00:05:53.065 --> 00:05:54.063
- Yeah.

00:05:54.063 --> 00:05:55.363
I can't either.

00:05:55.363 --> 00:05:56.496
I think that I'm not gonna see the movie.

00:05:56.496 --> 00:05:57.627
I can't.

00:05:57.627 --> 00:05:58.811
I'm not gonna Netflix
it, I'm not gonna give

00:05:58.811 --> 00:06:00.147
my money to it.

00:06:00.147 --> 00:06:01.727
- You know that if tomorrow, if tomorrow

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.985
every guy who was ever charged with being

00:06:03.985 --> 00:06:05.476
an asshole, and woman,

00:06:05.476 --> 00:06:07.773
people stop supporting their art,

00:06:07.773 --> 00:06:09.371
you know people would take a lot more,

00:06:09.371 --> 00:06:11.386
they would think a lot
more before they did stuff.

00:06:11.386 --> 00:06:13.370
- I think this has definitely taught me

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.296
to look into people, and who they are,

00:06:16.296 --> 00:06:18.339
before I support them.

00:06:18.339 --> 00:06:19.467
Kwesi, thanks for joining us today!

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:20.836
Yeah!

00:06:20.836 --> 00:06:22.914
(applause)

00:06:22.914 --> 00:06:25.013
Alright guys, so you know what to do,

00:06:25.013 --> 00:06:27.000
leave your comments below,
and we'll see you next week.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.667
(downbeat electronic music)

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.503
(screech of dry erase marker)

